//? Title: TSNE: inspectable affinities, Iris and Swiss-roll checks
//? Subtitle: Actual native state, retained fixtures and explicit limits
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Visualizing observations with several features requires compressing their
relationships into two coordinates. TSNE builds local affinities before
iterative layout; we inspect those actual weights before using four unscaled
Iris measurements and a known synthetic manifold.
)

\toc

> The method

t-SNE calibrates p(j|i) proportional to exp(−β_i d(i,j)²) so 2^H approximates
the requested perplexity, then P_ij=(p(j|i)+p(i|j))/(2n). In the embedding Q_ij
is proportional to1/(1+||y_i−y_j||²), and the non-exaggerated objective is
KL(P||Q). Its gradient is4Σ_j(P_ij−Q_ij)(y_i−y_j)/(1+||y_i−y_j||²). Momentum
updates use the configured learning rate; early exaggeration multiplies P during
its initial phase. This dense implementation uses O(n²) affinity storage and
O(iterations*n²*components) work. Perplexity calibration has a finite50-step
cap; tied distances can make the target unattainable.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/tsne_iris_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/stats/embedding_diagnostics.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::dstruct::DataFrame d;
    d.add_column("x", std::vector<double>{0, 1, 3, 7});
    dm::stats::TSNEOptions o;
    o.perplexity = 2;
    o.max_iterations = 0;
    dm::stats::TSNE m(d, {"x"}, o);
    const auto &weights = m.conditional_probabilities();
    std::print("| source | target | actual directed weight |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 4; ++i)
        for (std::size_t j = 0; j < 4; ++j)
            if (i != j)
                std::print("|{}|{}|{}|\n", i, j, weights(i, j));
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Four raw points0,1,3,7");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0}, "Actual directed affinity matrix");
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("{} retained rows", m.observations()));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/tsne_iris_tiny.svg");
}
```
