> Interpretation and limits

The models fit unsupervised host numerical layouts; labels and manifold
coordinates are held outside fitting. Species distances and axis correlations
are descriptive checks, not classification accuracy. Translation, rotation and
scale complicate direct coordinate comparisons; correlation is axis-dependent
and is not a rotation-invariant manifold score. Dense pair geometry is limited
to2000 rows and64 embedding axes; nonfinite features/options and distances
throw. Fitting remains finite-iteration optimization without a convergence
guarantee. Original raw Iris features, default settings, perplexity/neighbor
sweeps,400-point seed42 Swiss roll and PCA/MDS/Isomap controls are retained.
t-SNE random initialization uses standard deviation.01. UMAP min_dist has no
computational effect in this simplified kernel. Public affinity matrices are
borrowed read-only state from the actual fit.

Every figure is saved locally by its complete editable program. No separate
reconstruction supplies algorithm state. Counters describe the selected events,
not elapsed time or peak memory.

> References

- [van der Maaten and Hinton, Visualizing Data using t-SNE|https://www.jmlr.org/papers/v9/vandermaaten08a.html]

